## Migration Analysis

Your code has three patterns that break on .NET 8:

| API | Problem on .NET 8 |
|-----|-------------------|
| `Thread.Interrupt()` | Obsolete (`SYSLIB0046` in .NET 9); unreliable on `WaitOne` |
| `Thread.Abort()` | Throws `PlatformNotSupportedException` |
| `ManualResetEvent.WaitOne()` without cancellation | Can't be woken cooperatively |

There's also a **race condition** in the original: multiple `Enqueue` calls can signal `_newEvent` but `Reset()` + single `Dequeue()` may miss items.

---

## Migrated Code (.NET 8)

```csharp
using System.Threading.Channels;

public class EventProcessor : IAsyncDisposable
{
    private readonly Channel<string> _channel = Channel.CreateUnbounded<string>();
    private Task? _runTask;
    private CancellationTokenSource? _cts;

    public void Start()
    {
        _cts = new CancellationTokenSource();
        _runTask = Task.Run(() => RunLoopAsync(_cts.Token));
    }

    private async Task RunLoopAsync(CancellationToken token)
    {
        try
        {
            await foreach (var item in _channel.Reader.ReadAllAsync(token))
            {
                Handle(item);
            }
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException) when (token.IsCancellationRequested)
        {
            // Normal shutdown — nothing to do
        }
    }

    public void Enqueue(string item)
    {
        _channel.Writer.TryWrite(item);
    }

    public async ValueTask StopAsync(TimeSpan? timeout = null)
    {
        if (_cts is null || _runTask is null) return;

        _channel.Writer.Complete();           // signal no more items
        _cts.CancelAfter(timeout ?? TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5)); // hard deadline

        try
        {
            await _runTask;
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException)
        {
            // Timed out — loop was force-cancelled
        }
    }

    public async ValueTask DisposeAsync()
    {
        await StopAsync();
        _cts?.Dispose();
    }

    private void Handle(string item)
    {
        // your processing logic
    }
}
```

